msgid "Hamiltonian simulation {#hamiltonian-simulation}"
msgstr "Simulasyon ng Hamiltonian {#hamiltonian-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian simulation is a quantum computing technique used to model and characterize quantum systems based on their energy and interactions. It has potential applications in drug discovery and chemistry, battery development, catalyst design, advanced materials, solar energy, and the study of complex physical phenomena such as superconductivity. \n"
msgstr "Ang Hamiltonian simulation ay isang quantum computing technique na ginagamit para i-model at i-characterize ang mga quantum system batay sa kanilang enerhiya at mga interaksyon. May potensyal itong gamitin sa drug discovery at chemistry, pagbuo ng baterya, disenyo ng catalyst, advanced materials, solar energy, at pag-aaral ng mga komplikadong physical phenomena tulad ng superconductivity. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By simulating molecular interactions and the behavior of electrons and atoms, Hamiltonian simulation can help researchers predict material properties, understand chemical reactions, and identify promising candidates for new technologies. Common approaches include Trotterization, which approximates continuous time evolution using sequences of quantum gates, and sample based quantum diagonalization, which estimates the energy spectrum for a given quantum system.\n"
msgstr "Sa pamamagitan ng pag-simulate ng mga molecular interaction at ng pag-uugali ng mga electron at atom, makakatulong ang Hamiltonian simulation sa mga mananaliksik na hulaan ang mga katangian ng materyal, unawain ang mga chemical reaction, at tukuyin ang mga promising na kandidato para sa mga bagong teknolohiya. Kabilang sa mga karaniwang approach ang Trotterization, na tinatantya ang tuloy-tuloy na time evolution gamit ang mga sequence ng quantum Gate, at sample based quantum diagonalization, na tinatantya ang energy spectrum ng isang ibinigay na quantum system.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A typical workflow starts by mapping a physical system, such as a set of interacting fermions or bosons, onto qubits and circuits. From there, you can reduce the resulting circuit's depth and gate count with compilation and error-mitigation techniques, run the circuit on quantum hardware, and reconstruct the system's properties, such as its ground-state energy, from the measured samples. The tools on this page cover each of these stages, and the application functions listed here provides a single managed workflow for Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
msgstr "Karaniwang nagsisimula ang workflow sa pag-map ng isang physical system, tulad ng set ng mga nag-iinteract na fermion o boson, sa mga Qubit at Circuit. Mula roon, mababawasan mo ang depth at bilang ng Gate ng resultang Circuit gamit ang mga compilation at error-mitigation technique, patakbuhin ang Circuit sa quantum hardware, at buuin muli ang mga katangian ng system, tulad ng ground-state energy nito, mula sa mga nasukat na sample. Sinasaklaw ng mga tool sa pahinang ito ang bawat isa sa mga yugtong ito, at ang mga application function na nakalista rito ay nagbibigay ng iisang managed workflow para sa Hamiltonian simulation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping tools {#mapping-tools}"
msgstr "Mga mapping tool {#mapping-tools}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These capabilities specialize in mapping domain problems into quantum operators and circuits for execution on a quantum computer. Use them to represent fermionic, bosonic, or spin systems, and to compile the resulting circuits so that they run with less depth and fewer entangling gates on quantum hardware.\n"
"<CardGroup>\n"
msgstr ""
"Espesyalista ang mga kakayahang ito sa pag-map ng mga domain problem sa mga quantum operator at Circuit para maisagawa sa isang quantum computer. Gamitin ang mga ito para katawanin ang mga fermionic, bosonic, o spin system, at para i-compile ang mga resultang Circuit para tumakbo ang mga ito nang may mas mababaw na depth at mas kaunting entangling Gate sa quantum hardware.\n"
"<CardGroup>\n"

